{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","title":"Constructing the perpendicular bisector of a segment"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with segment AB. We want a line that crosses its midpoint at a right angle, using only a compass and straightedge.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Perpendicular bisector"},{"op":"figure","id":"construction","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.5,3.5],"y":[-3.2,3.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[-2,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[2,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"segment","id":"ab","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"}}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Open the compass wider than half AB. Keeping that opening unchanged, draw arcs from A and B, crossing above and below the segment.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"arcs","on":"construction","marks":[{"kind":"arc","id":"aup","center":{"at":"a"},"r":3,"start":10,"end":80},{"kind":"arc","id":"adown","center":{"at":"a"},"r":3,"start":-80,"end":-10},{"kind":"arc","id":"bup","center":{"at":"b"},"r":3,"start":100,"end":170},{"kind":"arc","id":"bdown","center":{"at":"b"},"r":3,"start":190,"end":260},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"hit":["aup","bup"]},"label":"P"},{"kind":"point","id":"q","at":{"hit":["adown","bdown"]},"label":"Q"}]},{"op":"text","id":"radiusnote","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Same compass opening"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Use the straightedge to join P and Q. Both points are equally distant from A and B, so their line is the perpendicular bisector.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"join","on":"construction","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"pq","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"q"}},{"kind":"point","id":"m","at":{"hit":["ab","pq"]},"label":"M"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"equalradii","anchor":{"el":"radiusnote","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"PA=PB,\\qquad QA=QB"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s4"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"49064095-e957-488e-a33d-a373f77330da","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The construction gives equal halves and a right angle. Why must the compass opening be greater than half the segment?","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"verify","on":"construction","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"m"},"label":"d"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"m"},"to":{"at":"b"},"label":"d"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"m"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"p"},"r":0.16,"label":"90°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"equalradii","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"AM=MB,\\qquad PQ\\perp AB"}],"checkpoint":null}}
